Oh - and you would have to know it was your pet for kicks to have this affect
- in other words, blindness or hallucination, etc., makes all kicks alike.

Thinking about this also made me think of a new piece of armor that might be
nice to have around: "Boots of Destruction".

Boots of Destruction would have the interesting effect of destroying objects
that you walk on or kick.  Stepping onto a pile of loot would dull blades,
damage armor, crush potions, crumple spellbooks and tear scrolls.  Kicking a
boulder would break it into rocks in a single kick.  Doors, altars, fountains,
sinks, all would be destroyed by kicking them, with various interesting
consequences.

For example, doors would come unhinged and fly into rooms or down hallways,
leaving a pile of wood chips wherever they landed.  The door would do missile
damage to whatever creatures it impacted.  Kicking a boulder would send rocks
flying everywhere, like an explosion.  Kicking an altar would do the same
thing, but there would be other consequences to that...

Kicking a wall would dig into the wall, but chips of it would fly back into
your face and body, doing serious missile damage.  It would take 3 or 4
kicks to dig one space into a wall.

Kicking creatures would have the effect of a good named weapon.  Armor
enchantments would add attack +'s to its effect.  Of course, if you were
to attempt an "instructive kick" on your pet, the results would be disastrous.

"You gently kick your kitten in the ribs"
        "- more -"
"You are pelted with debris as your kitten explodes!"
        "- more -"
"You are blinded by the kitten guts in your eyes"
        "- more -"
"You feel like a jerk."
        "- more -"

